How to automate any WebElement?
===================================
What is WebElement?
---------------------------------
Every GUI element is called Webelement(ex. textbox,link,checkbox,button,radiobutton,dropdown...etc)

In Selenium WebElement is an Interface

1.First Identify WebElement From the webpage
2.Perform action on Webelement


1.First Identify WebElement From the webpage
------------------------------------------------------
Selenium Identify any weblement based on Locator

What is Locator?
-----------------------
Locator is address of that weblement


Selenium Support total 8 locators
--------------------------------------
1.By id
2.By name
3.By className
4.By tagName
5.By linkText
6.By partialLinkText

Dynamic WebElements

7.By cssSelector
8.By xpath

-----------------------------------------------
In Version 4 Selenium Support Relative locator
--------------------------------
leftOf
rightOf
Before
after
nearOf


----------------------------------------------
Selenium Identify Webelement using these methods

1.findElement()
------------------
- findElement() identify sigle webelement
- findElement() return single WebElement interface object
- findElement() fail to identify element then it throws exception NoSuchElementException

2.findElements()
----------------------


